            "line_count": 8,
            "preview": "assertTimeoutPreemptively(TEST_TIMEOUT, () -> { // A single-permit semaphore whose period is too long to ever reset during the test, // so shutdown() is the only thing that can wake a blocked acquirer."
          },
          {
            "start_line": 54,
            "end_line": 55,
            "line_count": 2,
            "preview": "// Consume the only permit available in this period. semaphore.acquire();"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 57,
            "end_line": 68,
            "line_count": 12,
            "preview": "// This thread will block in acquire() because the single permit is already taken. final Thread blocker = new Thread(() -> { try {"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 70,
            "end_line": 72,
            "line_count": 3,
            "preview": "// Wait until the blocker is actually parked in Object.wait() inside acquire(). // This replaces a fixed sleep and removes the race that one could introduce. waitUntilWaiting(blocker);"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 74,
            "end_line": 74,
            "line_count": 1,
            "preview": "semaphore.shutdown();"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 76,
            "end_line": 78,
            "line_count": 3,
            "preview": "// If shutdown() correctly calls notifyAll(), the blocker wakes, throws ISE, and dies // within milliseconds. Without it, the blocker stays WAITING far past this join. blocker.join(JOIN_TIMEOUT_MILLIS);"
